  "liveNow": false,
  "description": "Readability defaults for the relations family, and the bugs behind them. Each new default is paired with a control that switches it off, so the change is visible rather than asserted: label truncation and overlap hiding, arrowheads, adjacency highlighting, a seeded (reproducible) force layout whose settling is not painted, link colour actually resolving to the endpoint colours, the sankey's vertical label position, edge values, split zoom/pan driven by panel buttons, and a second reducer that reaches edges as well as nodes. Fixtures are written in the field-based graph contract (data-plane/graph-wide.md) rather than Grafana's row form, so every panel reads on a host without the panel-transformation flag.",
